  - patches/0001-t2smp-zero-mask.patch: change alloc_cpumask_var() to
    zalloc_cpumask_var() so the offlined-cpu mask is zero-initialised.
    alloc_cpumask_var() with GFP_KERNEL does not zero the mask when
    CONFIG_CPUMASK_OFFSTACK=y (the normal case on x86); a stale-on-allocation
    mask would carry arbitrary bits, so the first suspend could try to add_cpu()
    CPUs the module never offlined - including intentionally offline CPUs.

